ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  allergy to bupivacaine\n-  pre-operative opioid usage within the last six months\n-  patients allergic to Percocet or acetaminophen\n-  patients taking tricyclic antidepressants (interaction with bupivacaine)\n-  vulnerable populations (prisoners or pregnant women)\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "- allergy to bupivacaine",\n                  "Eq-Operator": [\n                    "-"\n                  ],\n                  "Allergy": [\n                    "allergy"\n                  ],\n                  "Drug": [\n                    "bupivacaine"\n                  ],\n                  "Drug-Name": [\n                    "bupivacaine"\n                  ]\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "raw_text": "- pre-operative opioid usage within the last six months",\n                  "Eq-Operator": [\n                    "-",\n                    "within"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Temporal-Unit": [\n                    "months"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Value": [\n                    "six"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Comparison": [\n                    "within the last six months"\n                  ],\n                  "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n                    "last"\n                  ],\n                  "Procedure": [\n                    "operative"\n                 