ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n1. Moderate-severe uni- and bipolar depression according to the International Classification of Diseases (ICD-10)\n2. A Hamilton scale score (HDS-17) of ≥ 18 and/or a sub-scale (HDSS) score of ≥ 9 within 24-48 hours before the first treatment\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "raw_text": "1. Moderate-severe uni-",\n      "Eq-Operator": [\n        "to"\n      ],\n      "Severity": [\n        "Moderate",\n        "severe"\n      ],\n      "Modifier": [\n        "uni"\n      ]\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "raw_text": "and bipolar depression according to the International Classification of Diseases (ICD-10)",\n      "Condition": [\n        "depression"\n      ],\n      "Condition-Name": [\n        "depression"\n      ],\n      "Modifier": [\n        "bipolar"\n      ],\n      "Observation": [\n        "International Classification of Diseases",\n        "ICD-10"\n      ],\n      "Observation-Name": [\n        "International Classification of Diseases",\n        "ICD-10"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}<|eot_id|>']
