ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Age >18 years\n-  Diagnosis of BCR‐ABL positive CML blast crisis according to the WHO criteria:\n-  Blasts 20% or more of peripheral blood white cells or bone marrow cells or\n-  Extramedullary blast proliferation or\n-  Large foci or clusters of blasts in bone marrow biopsy\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "raw_text": "- Age >18 years",\n              "Age": [\n                "Age"\n              ],\n              "Eq-Comparison": [\n                ">18 years"\n              ],\n              "Eq-Operator": [\n                ">"\n              ],\n              "Eq-Temporal-Unit": [\n                "years"\n              ],\n              "Eq-Value": [\n                "18"\n              ]\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "raw_text": "- Diagnosis of BCR‐ABL positive CML blast crisis according to the WHO criteria:",\n              "Condition": [\n                "CML",\n                "blast crisis"\n              ],\n              "Condition-Name": [\n                "CML",\n                "blast crisis"\n              ],\n              "Modifier": [\n                "BCR",\n                "ABL"\n              ],\n              "Polarity": [\n                "positive"\n              ],\n              "Observation": [\n                "WHO criteria"\n              ],\n              "Observation-Name": [\n                "WHO criteria"\n              ]\n            }\n          }\n        },\n       