ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  No history or diagnosis of any of the following conditions: Chron\'s disease, bleeding disorders, gastrointestinal or colonic malignancy, Kidney disease, including kidney "stones" or hypercalcemia, Coagulopathy/hereditary hemorrhagic disorders/ or receiving therapeutic doses of Coumadin or heparin.\n-  Ingested certain medications (Calcium, Vitamin D, fiber supplements and Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs - NSAIDs) within 30 days of study start.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "raw_text": "-"\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "NOT": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "OR": {\n                        "left": {\n                          "raw_text": "No history",\n                          "Negation": [\n                            "No"\n                          ],\n                          "Eq-Comparison": [\n                            "history"\n                          ],\n                          "Eq-Temporal-Period": [\n                            "history"\n                          ]\n                        },\n                        "right": {\n                          "OR": {\n                            "left": {\n                              "raw_text": "or diagnosis of any of the following conditions: Chron\'s disease,",\n                              "Condition": [\n                               