ictions, return an empty JSON FILE {}\n- The entire text of the eligibility criteria must be included and separated by the logical operators, without omitting any words or information.\n- The output should only contain the JSON object, without any additional text or formatting.\n- Ensure that the JSON output strictly follows these rules and accurately represents the logical structure of the input eligibility criteria.\n\n### Input:\n-  Males, with at least a year of experience in heavylift exercises, age between 20 and 35 years.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "raw_text": "- Males,",\n      "Life-Stage-And-Gender": [\n        "Males"\n      ]\n    },\n    "right": {\n      "raw_text": "with at least a year of experience in heavylift exercises, age between 20 and 35 years.",\n      "Observation": [\n        "heavylift exercises"\n      ],\n      "Observation-Name": [\n        "heavylift exercises"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Comparison": [\n        "at least a year",\n        "between 20 and 35 years"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Operator": [\n        "at least",\n        "between"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Temporal-Unit": [\n        "year",\n        "years"\n      ],\n      "Age": [\n        "age"\n      ],\n      "Eq-Value": [\n        "20",\n        "35"\n      ],\n      "Life-Stage-And-Gender": [\n        "Males"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}<|eot_id|>']
